{"c":[{"id":"ca9af4201f2b1f56","sum":"B28-G2: Ask sentences in planner/says.ts; Jev confidence = top-two margin; routed producers hold offers; Fill all writes handoffs with writes:true; scope words are allowlists; VM walks judged by results.json; goal steps only via goalAccept; pid-posted keys skip the tap.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"b9c59a7dd2810fa8","sum":"B25-B29: Ask sentences in planner/says.ts; Jev confidence = top-two margin; routed producers hold offers; Not right = slip source row click; Router 1 flips near 0.5; scope words are allowlists; Fill all writes writes:true handoffs; undo trusts intended values.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"0816855b3eb29c3d","sum":"Ask sentences: planner/says.ts; Jev confidence = top-two margin; unrouted producers self-trigger, routed hold offers; Not right = click on the slip's source row; perch is a rim; Router 1 flips near 0.5; failed fills via fillFailed; wait for site.waitForLoad.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"5b436031a992daa5","sum":"Ask's sentences: planner/says.ts, sent as error.says. Pin setGeneratorClock offline. Jev Choice confidence = top-two margin. Intent writer: 8k tok/min, space evals 30 s. Unrouted producers self-trigger; routed hold offers (routing.idle). B27 memory sets: evidence/screen/b27.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"78eeba3d0e4f7ab9","sum":"Ask's sentences live in planner/says.ts (SaidError message, sent as error.says since H5); pin setGeneratorClock in offline measurements. Jev Choice confidence is the top-two margin (0.75 floor ~0.875 winner). Intent writer gpt-oss-120b: 8k tokens/min, space Ask evals 30 s.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"943dffc1dbc84f96","sum":"B26: Ask's sentences live in planner/says.ts; a SaidError's message is what the user reads (since H5 sent as error.says), its detail holds the check's text. Offline generator measurements must pin setGeneratorClock or cold first forms are cut short.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T224111Z-32ca3d0fc6e98438","text":"B26: every Ask refusal or question sentence lives in planner/says.ts; a SaidError's message is what the user reads and its detail holds the check's text (ids, provider errors). Scoreboards print both.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T224111Z-6a820f7b64075f54","text":"B26: offline generator measurements (scripts/realfill-budgets.ts and the like) must pin setGeneratorClock, or cold first forms are cut short by the time budget and the numbers vary run to run.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"47481f5f6fb24ec8","sum":"D2-02: Jev Choice confidence is the margin between the top two option probabilities (a 0.75 floor needs ~0.875 on the winner). Groq gpt-oss-120b, the Ask intent writer, allows 8,000 tokens/min; intents are ~2,000, so Ask evals space calls 30 s or get 429.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T233505Z-310484d235184787","text":"D2-02: Jev Choice 'confidence' is the margin between the top two option probabilities (raw answers also carry 'probabilities'); a 0.75 floor needs about 0.875 on the winner.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T233506Z-254786afcaf981c8","text":"D2-02: Groq gpt-oss-120b (the Ask intent writer) allows 8,000 tokens a minute; an intent is about 2,000, so Ask evals space calls 30 s or get 429 'unavailable'.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1f86caa19701c852","sum":"D2-02: without HelperOptions.routing producers self-trigger; routed producers hold offers (await routing.idle() then routedSettled). Duplicate naps after a merge go at the next note. B27: score B17/B18 memory sets with the relabelled copies in evidence/screen/b27/memsets.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"94b9c96f4bec8c25","sum":"D2-02: without HelperOptions.routing producers self-trigger (tests, evals); main.ts routes when Jev is on; routed producers hold offers, so await routing.idle() then routedSettled. I4: a merge of two branches that napped the same notes lists them twice until a note refolds.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T233521Z-ca79b84757c7cc74","text":"D2-02: HelperOptions.routing absent keeps producers self-triggering (tests, producer evals); main.ts routes when Jev is on. Routed producers hold offers (engine.release/dropHeld, openApp.showHeld, events.judge); await routing.idle() then routedSettled.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T233858Z-3b9ba7299adc0299","text":"I4: when two merged branches each napped the same notes, git keeps both naps and wake lists their lines twice (T2's 60b138f0/b105c8e9 vs H4's 7234fe4d); summem has no command to drop one, so fold before branching or accept the duplicate.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c7e9161a825c4d83","sum":"I4: after a merge with duplicate naps, the next summem note refolds and drops them; write a note and do its naps. B27: B17/B18 memory held-out sets label own First/Last name 'none'; score with the relabelled copies in evidence/screen/b27/memsets.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T234020Z-7134731208a83f08","text":"I4 correction: the next summem note after such a merge re-plans the folds and drops the duplicate naps (one copy left per line, checked with recall); just write a note and do the naps it asks for.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T235441Z-17480ff5b594d902","text":"B27: B17/B18 memory held-out sets label the user's own First/Last name fields 'none' (written when fill copied values only whole); score them with the relabelled copies in ~/.caret-run/evidence/screen/b27/memsets, whose about-fill-eval accepts expect first/last.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"dab2f5b7a08bdf02","sum":"U2-B28: Not right is a click on the slip's source row (keyboard: the fact's row in What Caret knows); stand-ins clip; debug JSON omits nil; perch is a rim on the task's window. Router 1 flips near its 0.5 floor; failed fills reach users via fillFailed; wait for site.waitForLoad.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"c8d5b05b4e63693d","sum":"U2: Not right on an offer is a click on the slip's source row (keyboard: the fact's row in What Caret knows); stand-ins must clip; debug JSON omits nil keys (.get()); the perch is a rim on the task's window, drawn only while uncovered.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"a6b54378f08f606c","sum":"U2: Not right on an offer is a click on the slip's source row only (NotRightTarget); its keyboard path is the fact's row in What Caret knows. Off-screen stand-ins (ScrollingColumn) must take the height offered and clip, or the knows window's footer falls out of renders.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T000002Z-0878a22fa544c193","text":"U2: Not right on an offer is a click on the slip's source row only (NotRightTarget, a tiny click panel over that row); no key is claimed, and the keyboard path is the fact's row in What Caret knows.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T000002Z-0ab9ad748298511d","text":"U2: SwiftUI's off-screen stand-ins (ScrollingColumn) must take the height offered and clip, as a GeometryReader does; a fixed-size stack in a flexible frame pushed the knows window's footer out of renders.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"52b95150f4d0fe88","sum":"U2: debug JSON omits nil keys (read with .get()); the perch is a rim, perch and caption on the task's own window, drawn only while Rim.seen says it is uncovered; corner perch and perch-avoid are gone.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T000002Z-69ceb492909786b0","text":"U2: the host's debug JSON leaves out nil keys (synthesized Codable), so a script must read them with .get(); memory_documents_walk.py misread a closed editor as still open.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T000002Z-b1b1695c4d5b6282","text":"U2: the perch is now a rim, perch and caption on the task's own window, drawn only while Rim.seen says nothing covers it; the corner perch, PerchPlacement and perch-avoid are gone (perch-avoid now answers with an error).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"49622ae7d74e40f9","sum":"D2-02: Router 1 flips near its 0.5 floor between runs, so diff per moment before crediting a recall move. B27: failed fills reach users only via Helper.fillFailed. B28: wait for site.waitForLoad after navigation; accept.ts cannot run executor.run (use fake-app.ts).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"ccba801a8aa9c8ea","sum":"D2-02: Router 1 answers within ~0.05 of its 0.5 floor flip between corpus runs; diff per moment before crediting a recall move. B27: a failed fill reaches the user only via Helper.fillFailed (planner/says.ts fillSays); ids go to warn.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T031924Z-459c6ef9ec89ae5d","text":"D2-02: Router 1 answers within ~0.05 of its 0.5 floor flip between live corpus runs (m02 0.52/0.49, m09 0.45/0.51); diff runs per moment before crediting a code change with a recall move.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T032639Z-5905894b0fafbfcc","text":"B27: a failed fill reaches the user only through Helper.fillFailed (planner/says.ts fillSays); its window and field ids go to warn. Early exits that called this.error published ids until afadd34.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"91fb33162eeab888","sum":"B28: after a fixture page navigates, wait for site.waitForLoad before the next site.command; accept.ts cannot run executor.run (watchInput gets noWindow), so test page-link VerbResults there and the executor with test/fake-app.ts.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T044215Z-74ca06dede7d18b3","text":"B28: after a fixture page navigates away, wait for site.waitForLoad of the landed page before the next site.command, or the command goes to the departing page's long poll and times out.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T044215Z-8ef7ae66324e8796","text":"B28: accept.ts cannot run executor.run: it first asks the native reader for watchInput and gets noWindow; check page-link VerbResults in accept and the executor with test/fake-app.ts knobs.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"09bf3ebde9a35d91","sum":"B28-B29: Ask scope words are allowlists; controls never ride FillField.value, Fill all writes handoffs with writes:true, ticks by boxKind; FILE_INPUT_SUBROLE = PAGE_SUBROLE.file; runs need watchInput ok; undo trusts intended values; choices go to askChoices consumers.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"fe681129ca145b17","sum":"B28-D2-04: Ask scope words are allowlists (whole grammar sentence only; EXCLUSION_WORDS drop name trust); accept.ts attach checks need a quiet Mac; controls never ride FillField.value, Fill all writes handoffs with writes:true, ticks by boxKind; radio peers by form owner.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"4b0ed465d296cebd","sum":"B28-I5: Ask scope words are allowlists; whole-form or section scope only for a whole grammar sentence; EXCLUSION_WORDS drop name trust; SECTION trusts fields of its meaning only. accept.ts attach checks need a quiet Mac (10 s timeout).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"e2fcc93ff7d0331d","sum":"B28: Ask scope words (planner/scope-words.ts) are allowlists; a whole-form or section scope is trusted only when the whole normalized instruction is a grammar sentence, a section only under one un-nested heading of the user's own. Searching inside failed open 8 times.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T044915Z-bf6a7f62ff27c59b","text":"B28: Ask scope words (planner/scope-words.ts) are allowlists: only FILLER may stand beside a whole-form or section phrase, and a source phrase must open with a preposition. Matching field labels in the rest failed open three times.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T060231Z-5982020e0a78f148","text":"B28: Ask trusts a whole-form or section scope only if the whole normalized instruction is a scope-words.ts grammar sentence, and a section only under one un-nested heading that is wholly the user's own. Searching inside after stripping sources/titles/quotes failed open 5 times.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"13bd30baef5a6991","sum":"B28b-I5: an Ask with an EXCLUSION_WORDS word gets no name trust; a SECTION phrase trusts only fields of its meaning. accept.ts --host-app's 1.5 MB attach checks pass the engine's 10 s timeout only on a quiet Mac (5-10 s at load 45); rerun when quiet.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T063813Z-3bd79ae87e6b8e79","text":"B28b: an Ask instruction with a scope-words.ts EXCLUSION_WORDS word gets no name trust (Jev confirms every field); a SECTION phrase trusts only fields of its meaning (isContactField; up top, my details: none). Restriction word lists stay open; each review found more.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T064425Z-3cff2ff04b6480fa","text":"I5: accept.ts --host-app's three 1.5 MB attach checks slow with load (I4 ~2 s each; load ~45: 5.1, 8.7, >10 s) vs the engine's 10 s timeout. The no-input drop ships the whole file before attach.ts refuses it, so it fails first; rerun when quiet.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0c305010b2d5a883","sum":"D2-04: controls never ride FillField.value; Fill all writes handoffs with writes:true; ticks by boxKind only (never widen by words); accept.ts runs executor tasks on page windows; radio peers by name and form owner, tree-wide.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"499a4d2aad1ced50","sum":"D2-04: a control's value never rides FillField.value; a Fill all writes controls whose FillHandoff.writes is true (writtenFields). A box is ticked by its label's kind (boxKind: only a question to the user); consent word lists failed open twice, so never widen by words alone.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T080809Z-f16da6d6064b889b","text":"D2-04: a control's value never goes on the wire as FillField.value (zod and the host decoder refuse it on any control but text); a Fill all writes the controls whose FillHandoff.writes is true, through writtenFields.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T080829Z-0265fdcfcf17917c","text":"D2-04: a box gets a tick by its label's kind (fill/controls.ts boxKind: only a question to the user may be written, a first-person statement never gets a value); consent word lists failed open in both reviews, so never widen the box rule by adding words alone.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"63c022257923320b","sum":"D2-04: accept.ts's fixture reader answers watchInput ok, so accept runs executor tasks on page windows (B28's limit is gone); find a radio's peers tree-wide by name and form owner, since a button can join its form through the form attribute.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T080829Z-0557296abbc22e11","text":"D2-04: accept.ts's fixture reader answers watchInput ok, so accept now runs executor tasks on page windows (B28's 'accept cannot run executor.run' no longer holds); page input still comes from the extension's guard.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T080829Z-c2d09e45a7621952","text":"D2-04: find a radio's peers tree-wide by name and form owner: a button outside its form element joins it through the form attribute. The walker's radioPeers and the content script's otherChecked both searched the form element only.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e46d241c907c7f97","sum":"H5-B29: protocol lines round-trip in the reader, host-only ones in host.ndjson; FILE_INPUT_SUBROLE = PAGE_SUBROLE.file; runs need watchInput ok; ledger 'after' is the intended value; numbers compare by canonicalDecimal; choices go only to askChoices consumers.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"b09b974152313c33","sum":"H5-B29: protocol.ndjson lines round-trip in the reader, host-only lines in host.ndjson; file inputs carry FILE_INPUT_SUBROLE (= PAGE_SUBROLE.file since H6); runs need watchInput ok; a ledger 'after' is the intended value, a differing read-back blocks undo.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"62ee8c52d89713b7","sum":"H5: reader Swift tests round-trip every protocol.ndjson line; helper-host-only lines go in host.ndjson. Chrome shows a file input as AXButton; page-link marks it FILE_INPUT_SUBROLE, which is PAGE_SUBROLE.file ('CaretFileInput') since H6's merge.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T081037Z-26c2ee6e4f3a2b49","text":"H5: the reader's Swift tests decode and re-encode every line of helper/fixtures/golden/protocol.ndjson; lines only the helper and the host speak go in helper/fixtures/golden/host.ndjson, which both read by path.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T081038Z-3552e4cc7d35ed42","text":"H5: Chrome's AX shows a file input as a plain AXButton; page-link marks page file inputs with subrole caretFileInput (FILE_INPUT_SUBROLE), which validate.ts and planner/attach.ts require for fileAttached steps.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f3f18eac67e68cd6","sum":"H5-B29: an executor run stops unless the reader answers watchInput ok (accept.ts's noReader answers it via e.reader); a write's ledger 'after' is the intended value, and a differing read-back sets mayIncludeInput, which undo refuses.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T081038Z-d40e9fcab32c6674","text":"H5: an executor run stops at once unless the reader link answers watchInput ok; accept.ts's fixture noReader answers noWindow, so a run there (the confirm-file check) answers watchInput itself via e.reader.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T092126Z-f0c295d458383a43","text":"B29: an executor write's ledger 'after' is the value Caret meant to write; a read-back that differs sets mayIncludeInput and undo refuses it. Journal rows without afterIntended (saved before B29) recover their confirmed writes as mayIncludeInput.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"2b825510be0b4a07","sum":"B29: number fields compare by canonicalDecimal for undo; 'without using X' restricts sources (tests say 'not from X'); a continued Ask checks fieldSeen around fill's Jev calls; choices go only to askChoices consumers (the host since H6).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"33a32dbecb06c39a","sum":"B29: page number fields (PAGE_SUBROLE.number) compare as numbers for undo identity through canonicalDecimal (Number() merged 2^53+1 with 2^53); sources.ts RESTRICTS matches 'without using X' too, so excluded-source tests say 'not from X'.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T092127Z-2a54c50194565255","text":"B29: page number fields (type=number, inputmode numeric/decimal -> PAGE_SUBROLE.number) compare as numbers for undo identity only, through executor.ts canonicalDecimal; Number() made 9007199254740993 equal 9007199254740992.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T092127Z-2d5fb1876e453777","text":"B29: sources.ts RESTRICTS also matches 'without using X', and such an instruction gets no source question; tests of an excluded source window use 'not from X'.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1c75543de1b1c0e8","sum":"B29: a continued Ask refuses a changed form via ask.ts fieldSeen (add whatever fill starts reading); questions with choices go only to a consumer whose hello lists askChoices (the host since H6); AskAsks extends AskRefused for older callers.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T092127Z-2ff420afa6ce639a","text":"B29: a continued Ask refuses a changed form by ask.ts fieldSeen, checked before and after the fill's Jev calls; three reviews each found something fill reads that the record missed, so add to fieldSeen whatever fill starts reading.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T092127Z-c755285b7eff0669","text":"B29: Ask questions with choices (planner/choices.ts) go only to a consumer whose hello lists askChoices; AskAsks extends AskRefused, so any other caller reads the old refusal sentence.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c895e0a6f9e3413e","sum":"H6-G2: VM walks judged by results.json; goal steps only via goalAccept, presses hand off; drafts are whole facts; pid-posted keys skip the tap; guest file URLs name real files; stop the router before Helper.shutdown; Router 1 notes in routing/; goals done with left[] empty.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"fe8ea3764a8fcfad","sum":"H6-B30: judge VM walks by results.json; alternatives never withdraw for room; goal steps only via goalAccept, presses hand off; drafts are whole facts; router errors are a missed budget; pid-posted keys skip the tap; unreadable clipboard items refuse paste.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"dbb04edae3a352a3","sum":"H7: judge a18_vm_walk.py results.json with vm_results.py; TextEdit fix ⌘Z is one pid-directed ⌘Z; alternatives never withdraw for room. D2-06/V1b: goal steps only via goalAccept, presses hand off, GoalRuns.blocked null after a segment; unreadable clipboard items refuse paste.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"238a84aaa66db02b","sum":"H7: a18_vm_walk.py writes results.json after each check (judge with vm_results.py); TextEdit writing-fix ⌘Z is one pid-directed ⌘Z, others AX restore; alternatives never withdraw for room (inline or capsule); undrawn offers withdraw; late draws publish(shown:false)+reveal.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"1cb02aaa5824eced","sum":"H7: a18_vm_walk.py writes results.json after every check (judge with vm_results.py, test with test_a18_vm_walk.py); a writing fix's Cmd-Z in TextEdit is one pid-directed Cmd-Z (nativeUndo) with no AX restore after; other apps keep the AX restore.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T102528Z-49569322ff77aac5","text":"H7: a18_vm_walk.py writes results.json after every check and in finally; VM jobs judge it with scripts/vm_results.py, never the transcript's last line. test_a18_vm_walk.py runs the walk against stand-ins on any Mac.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T102528Z-b2fd96251e54b1a0","text":"H7: a writing fix's ⌘Z in TextEdit sends TextEdit one pid-directed ⌘Z (UndoGrant.strategy nativeUndo, NativeUndoApps); nothing restores text after it is sent. Other apps keep the AX restore, which TextEdit-like apps record as a new undo step.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"95ce68e7dc925e47","sum":"H7: a18_vm_walk.py results.json is judged by vm_results.py; alternatives never withdraw for room (fitsInField picks inline or capsule, capsules below the caret line else above); undrawn offers withdraw; drawn-after-publish uses publish(shown: false) + reveal.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T102543Z-0a3850ef6a0fa08f","text":"H7: a18_vm_walk.py writes results.json after every check and in finally; VM jobs judge it with scripts/vm_results.py, not the transcript tail. test_a18_vm_walk.py runs the walk against stand-ins on any Mac.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T102543Z-4af89305464255b2","text":"H7: alternatives never withdraw for want of inline room: fitsInField picks inline or capsule; CaretLinePlacement puts capsules below the caret line, else above. Undrawn offers withdraw (notDrawn); offers drawn after publish use publish(shown: false) + reveal.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"180a63d9d112870b","sum":"D2-06/V1b: 'Continue' never classified; goal press only e:reveal on 'Next'; page presses hand off; only goalAccept runs goal steps, no taskControl resume; GoalRuns.blocked must go null after a segment or undo fails. Unreadable clipboard items refuse the paste.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"cf5de0df55b6d70e","sum":"D2-06: 'Continue' is unclassified at every press boundary (it confirms destructive dialogs); the one goal press is e:reveal on a whole 'Next'; page presses hand off. Only goalAccept runs a goal's steps; taskControl never resumes one; targets are Target.exact, no fallback.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T105430Z-1712f90f65a11b14","text":"D2-06: 'Continue' is deliberately unclassified at every press boundary (it confirms destructive macOS dialogs); the one goal press capability is e:reveal on a whole 'Next' (goals/capabilities.ts). Page presses are always hand-offs.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T105430Z-1ba2dff3c7f2e7e3","text":"D2-06: only a goalAccept (goalId, segment, digest) runs a goal's steps; a goal task (GoalRuns.owns) is never resumed by taskControl, and a pause stops it. Goal targets are Target.exact (key+role, a button's label): resolveLocally never falls back for them.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"2fca48002a55d2e6","sum":"D2-06/V1b: GoalRuns.blocked (inside authorize before every act) must return null once a segment ends, or goal undo is refused. A clipboard item with no readable type (a lone public.file-url) refuses the paste; lastInsertion.clipboardTypes shows what was saved.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T105431Z-2d9978b4db29946e","text":"D2-06: GoalRuns.blocked runs inside Helper.authorize before every act; it must return null once a segment ends, or a goal task's undo (undoBlocked -> authorize) is refused.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T110217Z-f50d1fce02c90ec1","text":"V1b: Caret pasted over a clipboard whose 2nd item held only public.file-url and the restore dropped it, reporting restored. Items with no readable type now refuse the paste; lastInsertion.clipboardTypes shows what Caret's save read.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c11a295989bc0680","sum":"B30-H7b: plan Asks become goals for goal hosts; name regexes stay case-sensitive; drafts are whole facts. Router errors (R2) are the host's missed budget; pid-posted keys skip the tap; RouteFollower binds by text digest; only ReconcilingClipboard.check snapshots.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"73770d76091cc26a","sum":"B30: plan-route Asks become goals for goal hosts (planAsk goals:true); keep name regexes case-sensitive (i folds \\p{Lu}). Goal writes skip Cc/Bcc/Subject, To = answered From. Drafts checked as whole typed facts; close holes with whole-expression rules.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"eaeefb243874759f","sum":"B30: a goal-planning host's Ask with route plan becomes a D2-06 goal (planAsk goals:true -> AskGoal, helper.offerGoal); others keep planTask/planWithCode. A JS regex with the i flag folds \\p{Lu} to lower case: keep name patterns case-sensitive.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T120548Z-9e86109ce30422ae","text":"B30: a goal-planning host's Ask with route plan is offered as a D2-06 goal (planAsk goals:true returns AskGoal; helper.offerGoal); other consumers keep planTask/planWithCode. planAsk overloads: goals absent/false types as AskDraft.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T120548Z-b6135cb945f89335","text":"B30: JS regex with the i flag folds \\p{Lu} to match lower case too; a case-insensitive name pattern let 'Thanks, I'll pay' skip Jev. Keep name patterns case-sensitive.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"d827b4876610494b","sum":"B30: goal writes never touch Cc/Bcc/Subject; To takes only the From of the answered message (drafts.ts senderOf, rechecked at accept). Drafted text is checked as whole typed facts, every digit in a fact; fix holes with whole-expression rules, never token allowlists.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T120548Z-c27c662d572bf540","text":"B30: goal writes never touch Cc/Bcc or Subject, and To takes only the From address in the header block of the message the reply window answers (Re: <subject>), rechecked at accept (drafts.ts senderOf). D2-06 scenes rely on mailWindow line 0 being its From header.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T120623Z-4f068d6de508aa09","text":"B30: drafted goal text is checked in goals/drafts.ts as whole typed facts; every digit must land in a fact, and a from value ref stands for its source window or memory. Two reviews found recombination holes: add whole-expression rules, never token allowlists.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ee5e6005a3f942f5","sum":"H6-H7b: pid-posted keys skip the tap (route through debug 'key char:x' to stamp latency); a router error is outcome error (R2), a missed budget for the host; bindings from sha256(text+NUL+'unknown') digests; only ReconcilingClipboard.check snapshots the clipboard.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"54a198c67235f383","sum":"H6: pid-posted keys skip the host tap (no latency stamp); ghost_latency_routing.py routes each key through debug 'key char:x' first. Since R2/H8 a failed router call is outcome error + failure, and RouteFollower treats it as that context's missed budget.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T132640Z-116806e783493150","text":"H6: keys posted with CGEventPostToPid never pass the host's event tap, so its latency recorder gets no key stamp; ghost_latency_routing.py routes each key through the debug hook 'key char:x' first, which stamps it, then posts it to the fixture.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T132640Z-ec39615ba3d313e7","text":"H6: the helper publishes a failed or low-confidence router call as a plain abstain (no reason on the wire), so the host cannot fall back on a router error; only a decision that never arrives triggers RouteFollower's budget fallback.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"40260a53530a61ef","sum":"H6: RouteFollower binds the reader's window id/key from a decision whose textRevision is sha256(text+NUL+'unknown')[:16]; empty fields stay tentative. H7b: only ReconcilingClipboard.check snapshots; every posted key asks mayPost; restored = byte-for-byte re-read.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T132833Z-3831e1a92c996341","text":"H6: the host can't compute the reader's window id/key; RouteFollower binds them from a routeDecision whose textRevision is sha256(text+NUL+'unknown')[:16]. Empty fields share that digest, so their binding stays tentative until the host's revision is echoed.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T133211Z-54e0f06319860375","text":"H7b: only ReconcilingClipboard.check makes a ClipboardSnapshot; the executor arms it before KeyType's inserter, every posted key asks mayPost, and restored means a fresh read at the restore's own count matched type for type, byte for byte.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"dcd30d5c9d57bc88","sum":"H6-G2: guest file URLs name real files; stop the router before Helper.shutdown; ghost runs use a fresh TextEdit; rig cua-driver alerts cover windows; replayed typing needs value+focusedKey together; Router 1 notes in routing/; goals done only with left[] empty.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"af620a5eca93aec7","sum":"H6-R3: guest file URLs must name real files; stop the router before Helper.shutdown; ghost runs type into a fresh TextEdit; rig cua-driver alerts cover windows; replayed typing needs value+focusedKey in one snapshot; corpus incoming-line moments use the fake clock.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"968935f1f64b4697","sum":"H6-H7b: guest file URLs: seed real files as Finder does; stop the router before Helper.shutdown in scripts; on-screen ghost runs type into a fresh TextEdit; in the rig, cua-driver get_window_state raises a covering alert, so read AX with a17-tool value.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"f9874c6fb70cb129","sum":"H7b: in the VM a public.file-url naming a missing file is seen only by its writer; seed file URLs as Finder does. H6: Helper.shutdown leaves the router live: in-process scripts stop it first (routing_option.ts stop), or a late observe hits closed stores.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T133211Z-f47f4f8a4eaf4829","text":"H7b: on the VM guest's general pasteboard a public.file-url naming a missing file is seen only by its writer; other processes (Caret, a17-tool dump) never list it, count unchanged (A17 race00, plain05-09). Seed file URLs as Finder does: NSURL of a real file.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T143020Z-7e9c54758649b0bf","text":"H6: Helper.shutdown leaves the router live: in-process scripts stop it first (routing_option.ts stop: shadow, cancel timers, await idle), or a late observe hits closed stores and ends the run ('statement has been finalized').","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"2bbdec88d0b9e745","sum":"H6/H7b: on-screen ghost runs type into a fresh TextEdit (caret-fixture's field gave few value reads). In the rig guest cua-driver get_window_state raises a bypass alert that covers windows (offers held covered); read AX with a17-tool value.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T143020Z-8eb592e9f22ab7a6","text":"H6: on-screen ghost runs type into a fresh TextEdit instance; caret-fixture's single-line field gave the host almost no value reads. With pid-posted keys both reader and host saw TextEdit's field come and go 20+ times in 130 keys.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T152850Z-7c0a9e0204dd886b","text":"H7b: in the rig guest, cua-driver get_window_state raises macOS's 'CuaDriver ... bypass the system private window picker' alert (UserNotificationCenter, layer 8); it stays up and covers windows, so Caret holds offers as covered. Read AX values with a17-tool value.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ac3096d5776075d7","sum":"R2-R3 routing: replayed typing needs its value in the same snapshot; no focusedKey makes Router 1 abstain; Router 1 skipped only for consentedCandidates offers (routing/consent.ts); run incoming-line corpus moments on the fake clock.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"8c07db9d1f57e7f4","sum":"R2: replayed typing must carry its typed value in the same snapshot as the text, or no breakpoint opens and no event card lists; a recorded snapshot without focusedKey makes Router 1 abstain (A5's offers-loop.ndjson lacked it until 831ab47).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T155131Z-2d735fed11dec073","text":"R2: scripts that replay typing must send a typed value (snapshot values) in the same snapshot as its text: a value that arrives after the sentence boundary opens no breakpoint, so the event card is never listed.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T155131Z-b3055d198779a6ea","text":"R2: a recorded snapshot without the reader's focusedKey makes Router 1 read 'the cursor is not in a text field' and abstain; A5's offers-loop.ndjson lacked it until 831ab47, which is why H6 saw the loop abstain.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"3b5d87e819a193ac","sum":"R2-R3: Router 1 is skipped only for offers consentedCandidates builds on a held offer's record (routing/consent.ts; those messages count only from a host session); corpus-eval --real-clock never waits the router cooldown, so run incoming-line moments on the fake clock.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T155145Z-05c6fed3ed39acff","text":"R2: Router 1 is skipped only for offers Helper.consentedCandidates builds on a held offer's own record (routing/consent.ts). Messages that write such records (skillAnswer, resume, skills/ save, watch role) count only from a host session.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T170330Z-3e0249266797e51f","text":"R3: corpus-eval --real-clock settle() does not wait the router cooldown timer, so an incoming line's later context is never scored; run incoming-line moments on the fake clock.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"592a384cd6680d71","sum":"R3-G2: jev.holding tests await a flush; Jev judges state on short criteria; Router 1's task question is separate; no routingContext for a plain caret; goals done only with left[] empty; pick goal values by quoted part; goal writes pass goals/gates.ts.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"71181bfecc426109","sum":"R3: await a flush not coord.idle() under jev.holding; Jev judges state against short criteria (rule in instructions); Router 1's task question is a separate request; corpus m36/m43/m37 misses are event-card code, not the router.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"5a582d7c7a76d2a6","sum":"R3: with jev.holding, await a flush not coord.idle() (a stale reply frees the slot); Jev judges the request state against short criteria: what it judges goes in state, the rule in instructions (task question with the sentence in the act option split ~50/50).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T170330Z-4f977dd1bf6c45f7","text":"R3: coordinator tests with jev.holding: a stale reply now frees the slot and the next field's call starts at once, so await a flush, not coord.idle(), while a call is held (idle would wait on the held call).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T170330Z-539f47d0a41290db","text":"R3: Jev (System One) judges the request state against short criteria; put what it judges in state and the rule in instructions. Router 1's task question with the sentence inside the act option split ~50/50 (r3 task-wording probe 8/14 vs 14/14).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"a2301c765553cede","sum":"R3: Router 1's task question is its own request after the outcome question (one shared state moved m34 write 0.75 to 0.32); corpus m36/m43/m37 misses are event-card code (no date anchor, no person), not the router.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T170330Z-75585e5911775e88","text":"R3: Router 1's task question (judge.ts) is its own request after the outcome question; with the offer in one shared state the outcome answers moved (corpus m34 write 0.75 -> 0.32).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T170330Z-9c33f255f5c1caad","text":"R3: corpus m36/m43 list no event card by the producer's rule (a conversation line's relative date has no anchor); m37 finds no person. Those misses are event-card code, not the router.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"21f781157288bdd8","sum":"R3-G2: no routingContext for a plain caret ('unknown' reads as caret); goals are done only with left[] empty; pick goal values by their quoted part; every goal write passes goals/gates.ts, and desk tests use test/goal-desk.ts standInJev.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"711ded7100cb3d56","sum":"R3-G2: RouteFollower sends no routingContext for a plain caret, so context.ts reads 'unknown' as caret; GoalProgress is done only when left[] is empty, and runs.ts owes every required or recipient field left.ts marks in windows a goal writes in.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T170330Z-dcc2d733c48b884a","text":"R3: RouteFollower sends no routingContext while the selection is a plain caret, so routing/context.ts treats the helper's 'unknown' selection as caret; comparing them ended every write session at the host's first sentence end.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T173412Z-100b242cff553f5d","text":"G2: GoalProgress finished is done only when left[] is empty (partial/handoff otherwise); runs.ts owes every field left.ts marks required or recipient in windows a goal writes in, and a closed window leaves them unresolved.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"9acdbaecfe2a51ce","sum":"G2: a goal value's display names its source window's title, so goal-prompt.ts says pick values by their quoted part; every goal write passes goals/gates.ts, lowerGoal needs askJev + ledger, and desk tests pass test/goal-desk.ts standInJev.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T173412Z-33695164e4940cad","text":"G2: a goal value's display names its source window's title, so live qwen3.8 matched v.display.includes('ORD-...') to the sender's email; goal-prompt.ts now says pick values by their quoted part.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T173412Z-c65516aec96de620","text":"G2: every goal write passes goals/gates.ts (never-typed, misfit + numberFieldMisfit, Ask's verifyWrites Jev question); lowerGoal is async and needs askJev + ledger; with no Jev a goal writes no copied value, so desk tests pass test/goal-desk.ts standInJev.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f34d5933ade42c31","sum":"G2-GW1: never widen restates(); page plans: WindowSel.page, hand-off row, page-planner.ts; host.sock in <home>/sockets; Jev daily cap; tab text via TabSource.viewFor; memoryRefOf; >20 fields in parts; Laya fixture-only, 512 tokens; with-heavy disk-est >= 8 GiB; closeTyping.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"4e94ccf8ea0486ea","sum":"G2-P4: never widen restates(); say 'at 3pm'; no default chat route; page plans set WindowSel.page; host page focus only from pageField; recheckFields drops failing fields only; page-link patches writes; window-left skips the browser; tab-left text via TabSource.viewFor.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"5ac6125c74b45908","sum":"G2-P2: never widen restates(); guest fixture at x=0; say 'at 3pm'; no default chat route. Page plans set WindowSel.page, page focus from pageField; tests never read GROQ_API_KEY; recheckFields drops only failing fields.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"afbc0885430f4042","sum":"G2-L1: never widen restates(); D2-06 scene 2 ends partial live. Guest fixture at x=0; no '--' in .entitlements; say 'at 3pm'; probe an EKEventStore if status flaps. No default chat route (--dev-writer); Gemma drafts few-shot.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"fdc428b470104795","sum":"G2-H8: restates() is a closed clause-suffix rule, never widen it; live Jev leaves D2-06 scene 2 partial. Guest 960x600: fixture to x=0; no '--' in .entitlements comments; event ⌘Z only after a verified step.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"6c27db8da975f9b4","sum":"G2: drafts.ts restates() is a closed clause-suffix rule; looser versions had 5 bypasses, never widen it. Live Jev confirmed Order number but not a reply's To sender or a derived event, so D2-06 scene 2 ends partial (evidence/screen/g2).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T173413Z-41b9cc8b0f0c0c83","text":"G2: drafts.ts restates() (skip Jev for a restated sentence) is a closed-frame clause-suffix rule; two reviews found 5 bypasses in looser versions (token sets, 'Avoid saying', 'NOT saying', 'provided'); never widen it by adding words.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T180513Z-82a90a8786c261a8","text":"G2: live Jev (Ask's yes/no value question, 0.75 floor) confirmed Order number but not a reply's sender in To or a derived calendar event for 'add this meeting to my calendar and draft a reply to Priya', so D2-06 scene 2 ends partial live; see evidence/screen/g2 jev-*-probe.txt.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"6064b9b210ca22b7","sum":"H8: guest is 960x600 pt, move a centred caret-fixture to x=0 or event cards find noClearSpot; seed-user-tcc.sh restarts tccd; no '--' in .entitlements comments; event card ⌘Z only after a verified step; calendar adds report written:0.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T182018Z-0c929a2ce63bdaff","text":"H8 VM: the rig guest is 960x600 pt; a centred caret-fixture executor window leaves every event-card spot covering a field (noClearSpot): move it to x=0 (fixture-ax move). seed-user-tcc.sh restarts tccd: running it while a TCC prompt is up shows the prompt twice.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T182018Z-327bc9cdd4327c33","text":"H8: an XML comment in an .entitlements file must not contain '--' (AMFIUnserializeXML refuses it and codesign fails). The event card's done line takes ⌘Z only after a verified step; the helper reports written:0 for calendar adds.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f5079ae2f5b9473e","sum":"H8-L1: say 'at 3pm' (an open AM/PM makes no event card); EKEventStore status can flap, probe a store. No default chat route; --dev-writer names one. Gemma E2B is a base model (few-shot drafts); deadlineMs is epoch ms.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"1c1ae9c575164268","sum":"H8: 'Thursday at 3' makes no event card since D2-03 (say 'at 3pm'); a card with no end asks how long. EKEventStore.authorizationStatus can flap notDetermined after a grant; host and reader probe a store instead.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T182018Z-f0560794b2ec28fa","text":"H8: since D2-03 an event sentence whose time leaves AM/PM open ('Thursday at 3') makes no event card; use 'at 3pm'. onscreen_acceptance.py still types 'at 3'. A card from a time with no end asks how long (30 min first, Tab takes it).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T182023Z-1d9814a513f71781","text":"H8: in a process running when Calendar access was granted, EKEventStore.authorizationStatus flapped notDetermined/fullAccess (VM) while a new store's calendars(for:) read fine; host and reader probe a store when status says notDetermined (no prompt).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f38309cb9958372d","sum":"L1: no chat route by default (writer routes null); a developer names groq:<model> or gateway:<model> via --dev-writer. Gemma E2B is a base model, so local drafts are few-shot; caret-local-model needs a grammar; deadlineMs is epoch ms.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T201333Z-b3e261779dc6c92b","text":"L1: no chat route is a default (WRITER_ROUTE and INTENT_ROUTE null, ASK_MAKER jev); a developer names one as groq:<model> or gateway:<model> (writer/routes.ts) with the helper's --dev-writer or an eval script's writer flag.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T201333Z-fdcac01d5471b677","text":"L1: Cotypist's Gemma E2B is a base model, so local draft prompts are few-shot documents (writer/local-draft.ts); caret-local-model refuses a request with no grammar. localTextRequest.deadlineMs is epoch ms, not a duration.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"00fd5ab66bea54da","sum":"H10-P2: page plans set WindowSel.page; host reads page focus from pageField only; label >80 blocks saved answers. Tests never read GROQ_API_KEY; new Ask makers join oneAnswer; recheckFields drops only failing fields.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"637b36e430ed09a4","sum":"H10-S1: page plans set WindowSel.page (page and reader windows share id and title); host reads page focus only from pageField. labelTooLong (label >80) blocks saved answers; old hosts lost the memory list on the answers doc id.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"1de8a2f92e9f1531","sum":"H10: a page window and its browser's reader window share bundle id and title, so page plans set WindowSel.page. Chrome shows AX no web content or focus, so the host reads page focus and frames only from pageField (PageFocusSource).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T203747Z-1771ea16bd50b7ed","text":"H10: a page window and the reader's window of the same browser share bundle id and title; plans for a page must set WindowSel.page or they stop as ambiguous.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T203747Z-8582de2538fa78c4","text":"H10: Chrome shows Accessibility no web content and no focused element while a page field has focus (VM probe), so the host reads page focus and frames only from the helper's pageField (PageFocusSource).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"4168398783b277b0","sum":"S1: fill throws labelTooLong for a focused label over 80 chars on a page with little prose, so no saved answer there. Hosts before H11 refused the answers doc id and lost the whole memory list; answers.md is listed only to savedAnswers hosts.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T204550Z-12e324b0b44784bf","text":"Fill throws labelTooLong when the focused field's label is over 80 chars on a page with little other prose (privacy prose share); saved answers can't be offered there.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T204550Z-3e3d4d7a0bdec136","text":"Hosts before v2/answers throw on an unknown memoryDocument id, losing the whole memory list; the server lists answers.md only to hosts with the savedAnswers capability.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"d6e449e5f141c6b0","sum":"P1-P2: tests never read GROQ_API_KEY (no-groq.ts); a new Ask maker joins planAsk's oneAnswer gate; recheckFields drops only a failing field; derived parts keep their line's label as context, else need an equal line.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"796fd5afdca57f46","sum":"P1: no-groq.ts fails any test reading GROQ_API_KEY even if caught (pass env objects). On W4 Greenhouse, recheckFill refused Fill all: a derived Country part needs a line equal to the span for a control with no label context.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T205140Z-7ef033e31edcf1b4","text":"P1: helper/test/setup/no-groq.ts (vitest setupFiles) fails any test file that reads process.env.GROQ_API_KEY, even if the throw is caught; pass explicit env objects to readKey/writersOnStart in tests.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T205140Z-d6ebebc54b7a4ea1","text":"P1: on W4's saved Greenhouse pages Fill all is refused whole by recheckFill (offers/fill-popup.ts ~218): Country 'United States' is a derived part of 'Location: Oakland, California, United States (...)', and a control without label context needs a line equal to the span.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"59654fc6f3466291","sum":"P1-P2: the heads maker is one answer, so planAsk gates it like the writer; a new maker name must join that gate. A derived part carries its line's label as context; recheckFields drops only the failing field; sourceHolds re-derives spans.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T205140Z-f4ebc7703c97844e","text":"P1: the heads Ask maker (planner/intent-heads.ts) is one answer, so planAsk gates it like the writer (oneAnswer = makerName !== 'jev': inferredAll, listsAll, confirmScope); a new maker name must be added to that gate or its scope stands unconfirmed.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T220819Z-519d2cf2c3af807c","text":"P2: a fill part derived from one 'Label: value' line carries that label as FillHandoff.context; recheckFields drops a field that fails its recheck and runs the rest; an unlabelled span inside a longer line passes only if derive.ts re-derives it (fill-popup.ts sourceHolds).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"9199063a79210b69","sum":"P2-P4 pages: page-link patches a verified write (one trailing walk); page Asks plan in page-planner.ts; window-left skips the browser's reader window; check undo over CDP; mergeCutWalk keeps unsent nodes; tab-left text only via TabSource.viewFor; freeze goldens via zod.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"04e70b9b4b65451f","sum":"P2-C1 pages: page-link patches a written control (one trailing walk); page Asks plan in page-planner.ts (clones refused); CfT calls Google via any proxy; guest Mail has no account; window-left skips the browser's reader window; check undo over CDP; goals leave restored picks.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"c4886c398087e862","sum":"P2-H10: page-link patches a verified write, walks once TRAILING_WALK_MS later; page Asks plan in page-planner.ts (gate 'fill' by identity: clones refused); headless CfT calls Google via any proxy (F1: browserService); guest Mail has no account (.eml: Add Account).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"353d6de786750cc3","sum":"P2: page-link patches a written control and walks once TRAILING_WALK_MS after the last act. A page Ask is planned by page-planner.ts with no writer; gate 'fill' is marked by identity, so propose refuses a structuredClone'd plan.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T220819Z-878907191e2eb647","text":"P2: engines/page-link.ts no longer walks after a verified pageWrite/pageSelect/pageSetChecked; it patches that control in the tab's last walk and walks once TRAILING_WALK_MS after the last act. Tests that expected a pageWalk after an ok write must expect the patch.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T220819Z-d4c70d849120ef71","text":"P2: an Ask about a page (goals:true) comes back as AskGoal.page and is planned by goals/page-planner.ts with no writer; its steps are gate 'fill', which only lowering marks (gates.ts markFilled, by identity), so GoalRuns.propose refuses a structuredClone'd page plan.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"dc7a4168ce70092a","sum":"F1-H10: headless CfT calls Google hosts through any proxy; the F1 sink files them as browserService(), not offsite(). The rig guest's Mail has no account (an .eml shows Add Account; its buttons label in AXDescription).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T224055Z-4008dd64a8214ebf","text":"Headless Chrome for Testing keeps calling Google hosts (google.com, googleapis.com) through a proxy whatever flags it gets; the F1 network sink (fixtures/web-form/oracle.ts) files them under browserService(), not offsite().","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T235610Z-e61928d562069b22","text":"H10: in the rig guest Mail has no account: opening an .eml shows the Add Account sheet, not the message; its SwiftUI buttons carry their label in AXDescription, not AXTitle.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"2eaf29a830280b84","sum":"H10-C1: a page's window just left skips its browser's reader window; F1's probe lags the DOM (check undo over CDP); 'from my notes' reads one resolved window; goal runs leave a restored combobox pick to the user and skip its dependents.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"62823ecfd9d9074a","sum":"H10-F1: a page's window just left skips its browser's own reader window (else Jev withheld at 0.65-0.77); F1's probe can lag the DOM after a burst of writes, so check undo by reading the DOM over CDP (page-loop-eval DOM_VALUES_JS).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T235611Z-1dede3bef7f49f2e","text":"H10: a page's 'window just left' (ScreenModel.windowBefore) skips the reader's window of the same browser; without that, Jev withheld page fills at 0.65-0.77.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T005116Z-802d1a3e98c70699","text":"F1's probe posts state with fetch keepalive and drops a failed post after recording it sent, so after a burst of writes the oracle can lag the DOM; page-loop-eval checks undo by reading the DOM over CDP (DOM_VALUES_JS).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0a881e10261f1993","sum":"P2-C1: 'from my notes' makes an Ask read only the window it resolves to (a decoy on the corpus); goal runs leaveFailedToYou: a restored combobox pick is listed (Executor.leftToYou) and dependents (state/city/ZIP) skipped; other callers stop.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T005116Z-d31529fbf9335d38","text":"P2 evals: an Ask saying 'from my notes' makes code read only the one window it resolves that to (planner/sources.ts); on the corpus that was a decoy note. Page-loop goal runs ask 'fill out this form', which heads settles as a whole form.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T021405Z-957fa1314ab52f39","text":"C1: goal segments run with leaveFailedToYou: a combobox pick the page put back (VerbResult restored) and read back unchanged is listed via Executor.leftToYou and the run goes on, skipping a country's state/city/ZIP (executor/dependents.ts). Other callers still stop.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"2dd914a0e2eed67d","sum":"P3-C1: mergeCutWalk keeps unsent nodes; attach rows for goalFiles hosts; carries span pages; says.ts never names Jev; freeze goldens via zod; tab-left text only via TabSource.viewFor; CfT tab switch via worker; fill budget load-dependent (budgetMs Infinity).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"777a097740a458a3","sum":"P3: cut walks keep unsent nodes (mergeCutWalk); attach rows only for goalFiles hosts, confirmedFile names its step; a carry lives across pages (carryOn); says.ts never names Jev; freeze golden lines through their zod schema (keys in schema order).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"b3b6ceb345ada2a0","sum":"P3: a cut reader walk keeps prior unsent nodes until a complete walk (model.ts mergeCutWalk); page goals get attach rows only for a goalFiles host (helper.ts filesFor); confirmedFile names the attach step; rows with no file drop from the run (runs.ts stepMap).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T021729Z-2e26e31d9e56986f","text":"P3: a cut reader walk (root null, stats.truncated) keeps every prior node it did not send until a complete walk (model.ts mergeCutWalk); inferring 'passed' nodes from the old order dropped a text area that a moved node jumped ahead of. Pages are still replaced whole.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T021733Z-eb34e4009fe61d9d","text":"P3: page goals get attach rows only for a host with goalFiles (helper.ts filesFor; in process via HelperOptions.goalFiles); goalAccept.confirmedFile names the attach step, and rows given no file are dropped from the run (runs.ts stepMap maps executor steps back to segment steps).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"b342efa209afe515","sum":"P3: a carry lives across pages until its goal finishes (runs.ts carryOn; pageWalked leaves a carried document alone); says.ts never names Jev ('Caret's model'); freeze golden lines through their zod schema (parse writes keys in schema order).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T021750Z-652b23e48a36082a","text":"P3: a carry lives across pages until a carried goal finishes (runs.ts carryOn); GoalRuns.carrying(windowId, doc) is true only for the document a carry plans, so helper.ts pageWalked leaves that page alone and takes any page the carry planned nothing for.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T021800Z-55351013aa4fbe71","text":"P3: user sentences in planner/says.ts never name Jev (test/says.test.ts plain()); Jev failure sentences say 'Caret's model'. Golden lines must be normalised through their zod schema before freezing: parse writes keys in schema order, so a round trip of a hand-built line differs.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c9f2c23e721be85d","sum":"P4-C1: tab-left text only via TabSource.viewFor(owner), never ScreenModel; CfT tab switches via chrome.tabs/windows.update in the worker (switchTo); fill's 15 ms budget makes probes load-dependent (budgetMs Infinity); line values read in TS (line-values.ts).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"298edb042298a31c","sum":"P4: text read from the tab left never enters ScreenModel; only fill sees it via TabSource.viewFor(owner). Headless CfT tab switches the extension sees: chrome.tabs.update + chrome.windows.update in the worker over the DevTools pipe (tab-source-journey.ts switchTo).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T032217Z-1ff9070e78c5cbc1","text":"P4: text read from the tab the user just left never enters ScreenModel; only fill paths see it, via TabSource.viewFor(owner) (engines/tab-source.ts). Never hand helper.model views or TabSource nodes to other consumers (router, event cards, shadow, transfers).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T032245Z-9aff69e636408257","text":"P4: headless CfT tab switches that the extension's tabs/windows listeners really see: evaluate chrome.tabs.update + chrome.windows.update in the extension worker over the DevTools pipe (fixtures/web-form/tab-source-journey.ts switchTo).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"05ed1f5f8cad4a0d","sum":"C1: fill's candidate budget (15 ms wall clock) makes in-process probes load-dependent (45-62 proposed under load ~30): compare at like load or pass budgetMs Infinity; fill reads values inside lines in TS (line-values.ts); recheck counts code-found ones via lineGives.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T032641Z-108c3beb10547e40","text":"C1: the candidate generator's 15 ms wall-clock budget makes in-process fill probes load-dependent: the corpus probe swung 45-62 proposed under load avg ~30; compare runs only at like load, or pass budgetMs Infinity.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T032641Z-52a641b0527a12b8","text":"C1: fill reads values inside lines in TS (fill/line-values.ts, candidates.ts windowValues), so the page-loop eval's replayed sources (values: []) now get typed values as the reader would give them; the recheck counts only reader values as typed, code-found ones via lineGives.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"387c54cf2e06fe08","sum":"C1-GW1: WARNS sentences go whole; page plans end in a hand-off row; host.sock in <home>/sockets; Jev daily cap, replay cache fixture-only, no distilling; memoryRefOf; >20 fields split in parts; Laya fixture-only, 512 tokens, 5 req/min; with-heavy disk-est >= 8 GiB; closeTyping.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"bcd860fe20ff53b5","sum":"C1-J1, H11-H13: page plans end in a hand-off row; host.sock is in <home>/sockets; Jev has a daily cap (CARET_JEV_DAILY_CAP); inject test pageFields over the debug socket; page offers are OfferSource.page and Tab sends pageInsert; never lockf build.lock in with-heavy.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"37e4af8adcf8abcf","sum":"C1-H12: WARNS-word sentences go whole; page plans end with a row:true hand-off; Asks read the tab left only at fill/pagePlan; host.sock in <home>/sockets (CARET_DEBUG_SOCKET=full); .fixedSize(horizontal:) clips wraps; no lockf build.lock in with-heavy.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"cd14b8843dd9d3ee","sum":"C1-I6: a WARNS-word sentence goes whole or not at all; page plans end with a row:true hand-off (no executor step); an Ask reads the tab left only at its fill step or pagePlan; ambient fill leaves a goal's page alone; the hourly budget holds pageWalked.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"2691af9702ea9f68","sum":"C1-I6: a value whose sentence holds a WARNS word goes with it as a required clause or not at all; page plans end with a row:true hand-off step ('You press <label>' / 'The rest is yours') with no executor step, so seg.plan.steps is one shorter.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T032641Z-df47ef2e50ca5a79","text":"C1: a value whose own sentence holds a WARNS word goes with that sentence as a required clause or not at all; sentence ends are conservative (lowercase word or digit before, capital after). Whole-line clauses cost corpus clinic-intake two values.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T062218Z-bb39f9f0467bc5ce","text":"I6: page plans end with a GoalStep row:true (kind handoff, 'You press <label>' or 'The rest is yours'); it is always the last step, lower.ts gives it no executor step, so seg.plan.steps is one shorter than seg.steps.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"740e3d49bc3a2762","sum":"I6: an Ask reads the tab left only at planAsk's fill step or pagePlan (owner: offer key or goal id); ambient fill leaves a goal's page alone (goalOnPage); the hourly budget (balanced 4) holds pageWalked, so the load journey lifts offersPerHour.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T062227Z-47ccc650cd567ff8","text":"I6: an Ask's tab read happens only at planAsk's fill step (fillModel) or in pagePlan; owners are the offer key or goal id; ambient fill/ready-on-load leave a page with a planning/awaiting/running goal alone (goalOnPage) and TabSource refuses an ambient read over a pinned goal.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T062227Z-6c026cce4f5fd842","text":"I6: page-loop-eval runs every page in one helper; the hourly offer budget (balanced 4) holds pageWalked before the ready-on-load check, so the load journey lifts offersPerHour; fill.load_held_<rule> counts holds.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c154314373edc26c","sum":"H11-H12: host.sock in <home>/sockets, release answers state+spend unless CARET_DEBUG_SOCKET=full; route page-engine test apply to its own helper; .fixedSize(horizontal:) clips wrapped panels (exact width); never lockf build.lock inside with-heavy.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"5e0b1d7fe48d167f","sum":"H12-I6: host.sock is <home>/sockets/host.sock; release builds answer only state and spend unless CARET_DEBUG_SOCKET=full (harnesses setenv it); onboarding auto only without --home/--settings; helper page-engine tests route apply to their own helper.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T035452Z-68fb99dd307065d5","text":"H12: host.sock moved to <home>/sockets/host.sock (default CaretV2/sockets); release builds answer only state (allowlist) and spend unless CARET_DEBUG_SOCKET=full, so release-build harnesses must setenv it. Onboarding defaults to auto only without --home/--settings.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T062227Z-7e02cffa1979776c","text":"I6: helper tests with a page engine must route its apply to their own helper (capture it in a local); a shared 'helper' variable lets an earlier test's trailing walk land in the next test's model.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"86a6db3d2adf8e6a","sum":"H11: under .fixedSize(horizontal: true) wrapped text measures as one line and panels clip: use an exact .frame(width:) with vertical fixedSize; build.lock is a symlink to heavy.lock, so lockf build.lock inside with-heavy deadlocks.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T063851Z-1e89e23b19f1384e","text":"H11: a SwiftUI view under .fixedSize(horizontal: true) is measured at its ideal width, so wrapped text counts as one line and the panel clips its top and bottom; give it an exact .frame(width:) and fixedSize(vertical) only (PopupView PopupWidth).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T063851Z-3a51e09ec56311ba","text":"H11: ~/.caret-run/locks/build.lock is a symlink to ~/.long-run/locks/heavy.lock; wrapping lockf build.lock inside with-heavy.sh (which holds heavy.lock) deadlocks while holding the heavy lease.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1ef09e53bf12acfa","sum":"J1-H13: Jev confidence (p_max-1/n)/(1-1/n); daily cap throws JevCapError; replay cache fixture-only; no distilling Jev output; test pageFields via the host debug socket; page inline offers are OfferSource.page; launchd argv0 is relative.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"d174639a9c85f705","sum":"J1: Jev confidence is (p_max - 1/n)/(1 - 1/n); a daily spend cap (CARET_JEV_DAILY_CAP $0.50) throws JevCapError; the replay cache takes fixture text only; TypeSafe's MCA s2.3(b) forbids distilling Jev output.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"987e4b1534648136","sum":"J1: Jev confidence is (p_max - 1/n)/(1 - 1/n) over n options (not the top-two margin judge.ts says; equal only for n=2); makeJevClient holds a per-day spend cap (CARET_JEV_DAILY_CAP, default $0.50) and throws JevCapError; vitest uses a temp spend dir.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T065440Z-6320f5713756d4a4","text":"J1: TypeSafe documents Jev's Choice confidence as (p_max - 1/n)/(1 - 1/n) over n options (docs.typesafe.ai/confidence), not the top-two margin routing/judge.ts describes; the two agree only for two options. engines/decide/confidence.ts computes other engines' confidence this way.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T065544Z-2b923d2a58b8f2cf","text":"J1: makeJevClient holds every request against a per-day spend file (CARET_JEV_DAILY_CAP, default $0.50; CARET_JEV_SPEND_DIR) and throws JevCapError (kind cap) past it; vitest.config.ts points the spend dir at a temp dir.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0d659675b89b1bba","sum":"J1: the replay cache and --log-requests take only fixture text (harness lists fixture window ids; the helper refuses the cache); TypeSafe's MCA s2.3(b) forbids distilling Jev output: train local models on Caret's answer keys or a permissive teacher.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T065553Z-29f2d5c421092ef7","text":"J1: the replay cache (engines/decide/cache.ts) and --log-requests take only fixture text: a harness lists its fixture window ids and says if its memory and plan text (window id 'plan') are fixtures; charged windows are checked too. The helper refuses CARET_JEV_CACHE.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T065553Z-310f47ee41817c11","text":"J1: TypeSafe's Master Customer Agreement s2.3(b) (2026-09-23) forbids using Jev's Output for distillation or to train an imitating model; train a local model on Caret's answer keys or a permissive teacher instead.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1e39825f89d0ff0d","sum":"H12-H13: inject a test pageField via the host debug socket (the bundled helper gets allowlisted env only); page inline offers are OfferSource.page and Tab sends pageInsert; a note window needs its own app in helper tests; launchd's argv0 is relative.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"379ec0af76ae5f62","sum":"H13: the bundled helper gets only allowlisted env (ServiceLauncher), so inject a test pageField via the host debug socket; page inline offers are OfferSource.page (native ghost clears skip them), insertsText false, and Tab sends pageInsert.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T080508Z-2110f7480275cbcf","text":"H13: the bundled helper gets only allowlisted env (ServiceLauncher: HOME, USER, LANG, TYPESAFE_API_KEY, CARET_ENV_FILE...), so a helper-side test switch never reaches it from Caret.app; inject a pageField through the host debug socket instead.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T080508Z-bc4a09143ef1ff5b","text":"H13: page inline offers use OfferSource.page (never .engine), so HostCoordinator's ghost clears on AX focus changes leave them alone; Claim.insertsText is false for a page ghost and PageInlineMachine sends pageInsert.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"940d166167db3d8d","sum":"H12-H13: launchd starts the agent with relative argv0 'Contents/MacOS/Caret' (use launchctl print's pid or lsof); in helper tests a non-page window with the browser's pid is passed over as Chrome's toolbar, so give a note window its own app.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T080508Z-ed6af011d8df3dcf","text":"H13: in helper tests, a non-page window sharing the page's browser pid is passed over as Chrome's toolbar (H10 ScreenModel.windowBefore); give a note window its own app (NOTES_APP) or TabSource reads the wrong tab.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T082217Z-6e9f887494c1affe","text":"H12: launchd starts the SMAppService agent as relative argv0 'Contents/MacOS/Caret', so pgrep/ps matching on /Applications/Caret.app misses the host; use launchctl print's pid or lsof txt. A fresh VM guest makes no helper Jev request (no transfers), fill or first look.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"11ec014c3ef4eda5","sum":"C2-GW1 fill+Laya lore: memoryRefOf for refs; >20-field forms split in parts; joined fills keep caller identity; gateway.only = provider; Laya fixture-only, 422s >512 tokens, 5 req/min (no Ask; slow-eval.sh, laya.lock). with-heavy: free disk - --est-disk >= 8 GiB. closeTyping.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"9061cdc44b6fa399","sum":"C2/F2/GW1 fill lore: memory refs via memoryRefOf; forms over 20 fields split into parts accepted and undone alone; joined ambient fills promoted to explicit, keeping caller identity; gateway.only names the serving provider; Laya is fixture-only.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"9663e92a97e02b87","sum":"C2 fill lore: build Step.memory refs with memoryRefOf, never by hand; countries come only from closed state/province lists; forms over 20 fields split into parts of <=20, each accepted and undone alone; page-loop-eval retries Fill all after 500 ms.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"cc84b3cf81253ebf","sum":"C2: build Step.memory refs (id[#part][~option|~date]) with memoryRefOf(m, conversionOf(control)), never by hand; placeWithCountry adds a country only from the closed US-state/CA-province lists, for fields asksPlace accepts.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T085433Z-15cdbeee47a325f7","text":"C2: Step.memory refs are id[#part][~option|~date]; memoryWrites checks text exactly and only options/dates through their conversion. Build refs with memoryRefOf(m, conversionOf(control)), never by hand.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T085433Z-9b6840ae7771fd2d","text":"C2: placeWithCountry adds a country only by the closed US-state/CA-province lists and only for fields asksPlace accepts; the engine still needs exactly one loaded option equal to it. About country is deliberately not used.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"d359c1b9ca63551e","sum":"C2: a page form over 20 fields is one goal with a segment per part of <=20 (reason moreFields), each run and undone on its own goalAccept; page-loop-eval's Fill all can race the page's ready-on-load fill, so it asks again after 500 ms.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T085433Z-a637346e142ef258","text":"C2: a page form over 20 fields is one goal with a segment per part of <=20 (page-planner parts, lower.ts cut, reason moreFields); each part runs only on its own goalAccept and undoes as task goal:sN. Fields past 4 parts are named as the user's.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T085434Z-d647567d5018f182","text":"C2: page-loop-eval's corpus Fill all can race the page's own ready-on-load fill (helper.fill returns null for a form in flight, no error); the row now asks again after 500 ms and logs it.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f8c7e4d7077b1a19","sum":"F2/GW1 fill and gateway lore: joined ambient fills are promoted to explicit; fill joins keep the caller's identity across waits; gateway.only names the serving provider; Laya is fixture-only (its endpoint permits training).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"bbf67222105d2e73","sum":"F2: fillRequest promotes a joined ambient flight to explicit before publishing, since ambient pop-ups fill no proposals. GW1: providerOptions.gateway.only names the serving provider from the model's endpoints API (laya-free is served by boundless).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T092359Z-18f5690369a8fa9a","text":"F2: fillRequest promotes a joined ambient flight to explicit before publication: ambient pop-ups do not populate proposals, so returning their FillProposal alone cannot serve handleFillAll. Different field scopes in one window wait and resolve fields again.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T094129Z-8c5d1007dd7df018","text":"GW1: the gateway serves convaiinnovations/laya-free through boundless, not convaiinnovations; providerOptions.gateway.only must use the serving provider listed by the model's endpoints API.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"79e694bb1404294d","sum":"GW1: Laya is fixture-only (its endpoint permits training): harnessEngine fixture provenance only, shipped apps refuse it. Fill joins compare selectedFormInputs after TabSource.readFor and keep the caller's reader/document/trigger identity across waits.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T100225Z-f4d02db1f4186bed","text":"GW1: Laya is fixture-only because its boundless endpoint permits training; use harnessEngine fixture provenance even with cache off. Generic clients without fixture provenance refuse it, and shipped-app markers always refuse it. Gateway Jev keeps normal sources.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T102153Z-a32a254ad92c6952","text":"Fill joins compare selectedFormInputs after TabSource.readFor: capped formFields can match scopes with different ranked controls. Preserve the caller reader/document/trigger identity across waits.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f3364d678b58484b","sum":"Free Laya 422s >512 tokens, JSON state, long options; 5 req/min: no Ask there (slow-eval.sh, laya.lock). Fill joins: one trigger, ordered inputs. with-heavy: free disk minus --est-disk >= 8 GiB; host build 3/2. Keep one of duplicate naps. Chrome insertText undo: closeTyping.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"97ddef9eec5e365c","sum":"A1/R1 Laya lore: free Laya 422s requests over ~512 tokens, JSON-object state and long choice options, and allows 5 req/min, so Ask cannot run on it; Ask scope is code's reading first (scope-reading.ts); run Laya evals via slow-eval.sh under laya.lock.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"b49778a23660a963","sum":"A1: free Laya 422s requests over ~512 input tokens and allows 5 req/min, so Ask cannot run on it; Ask scope is code's reading first (planner/scope-reading.ts), the heads 'reading' question confirms it, and ask-reading-eval.ts scores readings with no model.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T102251Z-3a116bbdf83faf20","text":"A1: free Laya (gateway, boundless) 422s any request over ~512 input tokens (489 ok, ~519 not) and allows 5 req/min per team; heads and corpus fill requests are ~2000 tokens, so the Ask path cannot run on Laya as built (evidence/screen/a1/laya-limits.txt).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T102251Z-6d4e95952b64681c","text":"A1: Ask scope is code's reading first (planner/scope-reading.ts; any unread word means no reading); the heads 'reading' question confirms it and intent.agreed skips confirmScope/sectionScope. ask-reading-eval.ts scores readings with no model.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"7bb813feffb3f3c1","sum":"R1: free Laya 422s JSON-object state and choice options over ~300 chars, so Ask-led evals there mostly fail; helper/scripts/slow-eval.sh runs eval sets on Laya in the background (a 429 ends the pass); queue on lockf -k ~/.caret-run/locks/laya.lock.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T102855Z-241459cd7cad2754","text":"R1: free Laya gives HTTP 422 for a JSON-object state (harness.ts layaState sends JSON text) and for a choice question whose options total over ~300 chars (heads' scope: 634), so Ask-led evals on Laya are mostly rejected (evidence/screen/r1/probe).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T102855Z-7e60ee41200b62c5","text":"R1: helper/scripts/slow-eval.sh runs all eval sets on Laya in the background; a 429 ends the pass and the set reruns from the replay cache. Other Laya users queue on lockf -k ~/.caret-run/locks/laya.lock; rejected requests replay from cache/failures.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"74a3e62ead206367","sum":"Fill joins need one trigger and ordered selectedFormInputs. with-heavy needs free disk minus --est-disk >= 8 GiB (swap counts): ask 3 mem/2 disk for a host build. Merged v2/* may hold a note in two naps; keep one. Chrome joins insertText to the typing undo step: closeTyping.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"8208911c044286ba","sum":"Fill joins need the same trigger and ordered selectedFormInputs. H13: with-heavy refuses unless free disk minus --est-disk stays >= 8 GiB (swap growth counts), so ask the smallest honest estimate (a host build: 3 mem / 2 disk).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T114711Z-5f2b276e7a41de4a","text":"Fill joins require the same trigger and ordered selectedFormInputs: descriptor admission can omit different fields even when input sets match. Different triggers wait with their own captured identity.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T132506Z-afeea7cd00f9f436","text":"H13: with-heavy refuses unless free disk minus your --est-disk stays >= 8 GiB, so at about 10 GiB free a 2 GiB build waits; ask for the smallest honest estimate (harness build 3 mem / 2 disk), and swap growth on this Mac eats the same disk.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"2aa517edf32bae42","sum":"I7: merged v2/* can hold one note in naps on both sides; keep one nap. a1-ask-reading once lost names at load ~11. Chrome joins insertText to the open typing undo step (one Cmd-Z took typed text too); setting the caret by script first closes it (insert.ts closeTyping).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T133620Z-cd21a7d05fec9102","text":"I7: merged v2/* branches can hold the same notes in naps on both sides (clean git merge, wake shows them twice); find leaves in two .tree files, keep one nap. a1-ask-reading 'acts on code's reading' lost names once in a default-worker suite at load ~11.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T161827Z-f17cd09096e8e827","text":"Chrome joins execCommand('insertText') to the open typing undo step, so one Cmd-Z also removed typed text in a contenteditable. Setting the caret by script where it already is closes the step: extension/src/content/insert.ts closeTyping.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
